Fix ``isinstance()`` and ``issubclass()`` inference when the classinfo is a
PEP 604 union, e.g. ``isinstance(x, int | str)``. Such calls previously
always inferred ``False`` even when the runtime result is ``True``, and an
``if isinstance(x, int | str):`` constraint discarded every possible value
of ``x``. Unions now behave like the tuple of their members, including the
``None`` member of unions such as ``int | None``.

Refs #3453
